      tip: "Put cost per resolved task on the same dashboard as quality. A cheaper model that resolves fewer tickets can cost more per ticket.",
      faq: [['How do you compute cost per request?', '(Input tokens × input price + output tokens × output price) ÷ 1,000,000 with per-million prices.'], ['Why do agents surprise budgets?', 'They make many model calls per task, with long tails.'], ['What hidden traffic costs money?', 'Evals, shadow traffic, retries, guardrails, and embeddings.'], ['Plan capacity for averages or peaks?', 'Peaks, with headroom.'], ['What is the most useful cost metric?', 'Cost per resolved task or unit of value.']],
      ex: { prompt: 'Write monthlyCost(c) where c has requestsPerDay, inputTokens, outputTokens, inputPrice, outputPrice (dollars per million tokens), and optional cacheHitRate (default 0). Cost per request is (inputTokens × inputPrice + outputTokens × outputPrice) / 1e6. Return requestsPerDay × 30 × (1 − cacheHitRate) × cost per request, rounded to 2 decimal places.', fn: 'monthlyCost', params: 'c', cases: [{ args: [{ requestsPerDay: 10000, inputTokens: 2000, outputTokens: 400, inputPrice: 3, outputPrice: 15 }], expect: 3600 }, { args: [{ requestsPerDay: 10000, inputTokens: 2000, outputTokens: 400, inputPrice: 3, outputPrice: 15, cacheHitRate: 0.25 }], expect: 2700 }], solution: `function monthlyCost(c){const per=(c.inputTokens*c.inputPrice+c.outputTokens*c.outputPrice)/1e6;return Math.round(c.requestsPerDay*30*(1-(c.cacheHitRate||0))*per*100)/100}`, hint: 'Per-request cost times monthly requests that miss the cache.' },
